  ],
  "equipment_type": "Air handling / make-up air unit controller (I/O and expansion modules)",
  "applies_to": "Engineered Air appliances (air handlers, make-up air, indirect and direct gas-fired heaters, DX and energy recovery units) built with the CenCon controller, version 3.0.0 or later.",
  "summary": "CenCon is Engineered Air's unit controller, with BACnet MS/TP (19200 or 38400 baud), BACnet IP and Modbus RTU. It works as a virtual BACnet gateway: the CenCon device (Gateway ID + 1) reports the main sensors, analog outputs, fan, damper and alarm relays and the safety inputs, and each fitted expansion module (DX cooling, indirect and direct gas heat, gas humidifier, energy recovery wheel, electric heat, spare I/O, combustion blower and pressure) appears as its own device. All objects here are read-only; commands go to the CenCon_SW device.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP",
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": "CenCon version 3.0.0 or higher",
  "default_device_instance": "CenCon = Gateway ID + 1 (default 270001); modules Gateway ID + 2 to + 31",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Each bracketed tag in a description names the virtual BACnet device: CenCon = Gateway ID + 1, C_XM + 2, J_XM + 6, G_XM + 8, M_XM + 10, S_XM + 12, H_XM + 14, ER_XM + 16, XP_XM + 17 to 20, CD_XM + 21, P_XM + 24 (more CD/P modules at + 22, 23, 25-31). The same object type and instance repeats on different devices.",
    "Module devices appear only when that expansion module is fitted.",
    "Temperatures marked 'value x10' are integers in tenths of a degree F; most other analogs are raw signals in mV or kOhm.",
    "The XP_XM table gives only terminal names (S1, AI1-AI4, AO1-AO2, DI1-DI4, DO1-DO4).",
    "Points marked (FUTURE) in the manual are listed as printed.",
    "Source: CenCon and module tables, pages 9-14 of IOM65 R106 (152 objects)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "CenCon Communication Manual for Modbus and BACnet (MSTP and IP)",
